    test: per-process scratch dirs for duckdb query fixtures (cross-process race)
    
    The four RETR/query test files created fixed dirs under process.cwd()
    (test-memory, -attr, -recency, -timerange) and wiped them in beforeEach/
    afterEach. Any two concurrent vitest PROCESSES (two gitreins judges, or a
    judge plus a dev run) raced on the same dirs: one process's cleanup deleted
    the partition another was mid-query, producing IO 'No files found' errors
    and cascading order-assertion failures. This is what failed DF-0919-02/03
    tier1 and looked like a 'flaky heartbeat' — the OPS-007 stall widening
    (2eb0bbd) helps its own timing margin, but the root cause was fixture
    collisions, now isolated via fs.mkdtemp per process in os.tmpdir.
    
    Verified: 4 files pass solo (35/35), pass as two CONCURRENT vitest
    processes, and the full suite is green (155/1212).
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
